# Team assignment

StudyNest is split into three member folders so each student owns a clear part of the project.

## Member 1 - Frontend Developer

Folder: `member-1-frontend`

Technology: React, HTML, CSS, JavaScript, Vite

Build these screens:

1. Login page and Sign up page with email
2. Home with student name and wallpaper
3. Summariser (500 word limit, PDF / ZIP / TXT)
4. Quiz generator (up to 20 MCQs A B C D)
5. Result page with time and attempt count
6. Tools with unique icons
   - Flash card generator
   - Paragraph to bullets
   - Maths text to algebra / geometry diagram
7. Settings: revision mode, dark/light mode, wallpaper photo
8. Daily reminder timer alarm
9. Weekly report
10. Monthly report
11. Daily task rewards in points
12. User history

## Member 2 - Backend Developer

Folder: `member-2-backend`

Technology: Spring Boot (Java), MySQL (H2 for local demo)

Build:

- Email authentication (JWT)
- All REST APIs used by Member 1
- Database tables and connections
- File upload handling for PDF / TXT / ZIP
- Calls to Member 3 AI service

## Member 3 - AI Developer

Folder: `member-3-ai`

Technology: Python FastAPI, IBM Granite / watsonx.ai, Node/React integration via REST

Build:

- Summariser
- Quiz generator
- Flash cards
- Paragraph to bullets
- Maths diagram SVG
- Optional IBM watsonx credentials via `.env.example`

## Integration contract

Frontend talks only to `/api`.

Backend talks to AI at `http://127.0.0.1:5000`.
